# --- ORACLE ---
# Runtime data lives OUTSIDE the repo (see docs/TECH_STACK.md "Data locations").
# Anything that lands here anyway must not be committed.

# Logs: directory structure is tracked, contents are not.
logs/**
!logs/**/
!logs/**/.gitkeep
!logs/README.md
!logs/development/*.md
# Measurement output that a dev log cites. A record that points at a file nobody else
# has is not a record — these are small (a few KB), they are the evidence behind a
# number in docs/, and they are exactly as durable as the log that references them.
!logs/measurements/*.json
!logs/measurements/*.txt

# Local state / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
config/local.*
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite3
secrets/
.oracle/
# ...except a project's own pipelines, which are source rather than state (PIPELINES.md
# §2). A workflow that decides what runs unattended belongs in review and in history, and
# an ignored one is invisible to both and lost on a clone. ORACLE still treats a pipeline
# found here as untrusted repository content whether or not it is tracked.
!.oracle/pipelines/
!.oracle/pipelines/**

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# Node / frontend
node_modules/
.vite/
apps/*/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Tauri / Rust
target/
apps/desktop/src-tauri/gen/

# Models & indexes (multi-GB, never committed)
models/
*.gguf
*.onnx

# OS / editor
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
